;; A.0.1.1.1 — Organizational Alignment
(: organizational-alignment Term)
(term organizational-alignment "Organizational Alignment")
(defined-at organizational-alignment "4f6fda1e-7450-4065-8095-e93cb10b3a2a")
(defined-in organizational-alignment atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash organizational-alignment "c80db34240032af33678c46739a27fed2dafa3cc7b0ead7212273c50c9f95eec")
(definition organizational-alignment "Organizational alignment is a traditional business concept and can be described as the process of implementing strategies and philosophies to ensure that each member of an organization, from entry-level positions to executive managers, shares a common goal and vision for the success of an organization.")

;; A.0.1.1.2 — Ecosystem Intelligence
(: ecosystem-intelligence Term)
(term ecosystem-intelligence "Ecosystem Intelligence")
(defined-at ecosystem-intelligence "5e2e1397-ff87-43ce-a742-e5a68dc89a44")
(defined-in ecosystem-intelligence atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash ecosystem-intelligence "a12961035094f8ed8d019b2f6d9ace0ff1ba7db26407b8b70859c081ec40e374")
(definition ecosystem-intelligence "\"Ecosystem Intelligence\" characterizes a decentralized ecosystem as a single entity acting with a greater or lesser amount of intelligence. Ecosystem Intelligence is not merely determined by the sum of the intelligence of each of its constituent parts, but rather the alignment of these parts. Counterintuitively, very intelligent, but spiritually misaligned participants in a decentralized ecosystem will actually lower Ecosystem Intelligence.")

;; A.0.1.1.3 — Aligned Structure
(: aligned-structure Term)
(term aligned-structure "Aligned Structure")
(defined-at aligned-structure "fad68392-c852-4102-81fd-2a4037be38f9")
(defined-in aligned-structure atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash aligned-structure "da359259b0c1a9aca2e43de475b3dc0550f22fb6194c6f86d01a4a08776c53b8")
(definition aligned-structure "An aligned structure is a network, ecosystem, entity, or organization that actively employs Alignment Engineering.")
(mentions aligned-structure alignment-engineering)

;; A.0.1.1.4 — Universal Alignment
(: universal-alignment Term)
(term universal-alignment "Universal Alignment")
(defined-at universal-alignment "9f953b73-566e-4428-a9d2-e179513c3371")
(defined-in universal-alignment atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash universal-alignment "a381d6c3f3d5b6b0a2e331a7b333a717290fa2c5ce06ad24f4ea7de89011b397")
(definition universal-alignment "Universal Alignment refers to an actor's holistic understanding of their connection to their environment or context. This enables them to anticipate how their actions influence everything around them, including the second-order effects that impact them in return. This holistic understanding is rooted in the context of human morality, values, and the natural world. An actor who is universally aligned can grasp the intent behind universally aligned rules and identify discrepancies between the technical incentives of rules and their universal purpose. An action that is in opposition to Universal Alignment constitutes misalignment. Preventing misalignment is the fundamental objective of Alignment Engineering and Alignment Artifacts.")
(mentions universal-alignment alignment-artifact)
(mentions universal-alignment alignment-engineering)
(mentions universal-alignment misalignment)

;; A.0.1.1.5 — Universal Alignment Assumption
(: universal-alignment-assumption Term)
(term universal-alignment-assumption "Universal Alignment Assumption")
(defined-at universal-alignment-assumption "2ea378ee-9b12-4e09-9f42-0c6ec65ef33b")
(defined-in universal-alignment-assumption atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash universal-alignment-assumption "eb7a95901e1b2f1237fd6235fb676c3826817867d881722466d87345b62bef82")
(definition universal-alignment-assumption "Universal Alignment is a spectrum, and actors are more or less Universally Aligned.\n\nIn theory, Universal Alignment is absolute, but in practice it cannot be measured deterministically and thus practically will always be subject to debate and changes over time. Alignment Engineering aims to minimize the degree that actors experience their own, and others’, Universal Alignment changing over time.\n\nThe Universal Alignment Assumption holds that the outcomes of Alignment Engineering - namely, the Alignment Artifacts or rules themselves - always have the spirit, or underlying intent, to serve human values and promote the public good within a specific context.")
(mentions universal-alignment-assumption alignment-artifact)
(mentions universal-alignment-assumption alignment-engineering)
(mentions universal-alignment-assumption universal-alignment)

;; A.0.1.1.6 — Alignment Artifact Strength
(: alignment-artifact-strength Term)
(term alignment-artifact-strength "Alignment Artifact Strength")
(defined-at alignment-artifact-strength "3b712852-26a9-4fb9-8a9a-ebf2332d3efa")
(defined-in alignment-artifact-strength atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash alignment-artifact-strength "ddc6a3754d8ed8e49cc024a30ec9d14198ab6dadfef5d2ab2c2509c5d63aaeb6")
(definition alignment-artifact-strength "The strength of an Alignment Artifact dictates the minimum level of Universal Alignment that an actor must possess in order to take actions that are universally aligned when interacting with the Artifact.\n\nAlignment Artifact Strength is enhanced by ensuring that Ecosystem Intelligence evolves such that each actor’s self-interested incentives correspond as precisely as possible with requirements of Universal Alignment. This alignment minimizes the additional effort, or \"inner incentive\", that an actor must exert to overcome misalignment.\n\nThe stronger an Alignment Artifact, the less inner incentive that an actor need possess to take actions that are universally aligned.")
(mentions alignment-artifact-strength alignment-artifact)
(mentions alignment-artifact-strength ecosystem-intelligence)
(mentions alignment-artifact-strength inner-incentive)
(mentions alignment-artifact-strength misalignment)
(mentions alignment-artifact-strength universal-alignment)

;; A.0.1.1.7 — Inner Incentive
(: inner-incentive Term)
(term inner-incentive "Inner Incentive")
(defined-at inner-incentive "102b11a3-9c8c-423e-bd5f-a0988048f11e")
(defined-in inner-incentive atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash inner-incentive "e521eb0aa17f984edd5622eb456796ea74505dde62163e0ca8277409a6265121")
(definition inner-incentive "Inner incentive is the second-order incentive that a universally aligned actor uses to counteract the first-order (or self-interested) incentives that exist pre-Alignment Engineering or that arise from a misaligned structure.")
(mentions inner-incentive alignment-engineering)

;; A.0.1.1.8 — Alignment Engineering
(: alignment-engineering Term)
(term alignment-engineering "Alignment Engineering")
(defined-at alignment-engineering "3caef1a5-8d59-4a00-846c-fc0f060b3f05")
(defined-in alignment-engineering atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash alignment-engineering "f589d249fb9ce4791d0adabe8a13e0b0089c409ed9b8ab50a447acb35a7e5dc2")
(definition alignment-engineering "Alignment Engineering is a philosophy of organizational design introduced through the Atlas. It aims to anchor internally sustainable Ecosystem Intelligence within Alignment Artifacts that embody recursive trends towards increased Alignment Artifact Strength over time.")
(mentions alignment-engineering alignment-artifact)
(mentions alignment-engineering alignment-artifact-strength)
(mentions alignment-engineering ecosystem-intelligence)
(mentions alignment-engineering the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.9 — Letter Of The Rule Vs Spirit Of The Rule
(: letter-of-the-rule-vs-spirit-of-the-rule Term)
(term letter-of-the-rule-vs-spirit-of-the-rule "Letter Of The Rule Vs Spirit Of The Rule")
(defined-at letter-of-the-rule-vs-spirit-of-the-rule "ff16fd74-3a81-4cac-92b4-1208d4d9f337")
(defined-in letter-of-the-rule-vs-spirit-of-the-rule atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash letter-of-the-rule-vs-spirit-of-the-rule "7e4aa98332eae6164effa18dd253745493f3b5419a88588b323f46cfd8db049f")
(definition letter-of-the-rule-vs-spirit-of-the-rule "The distinction between the \"letter of the rule\" and the \"spirit of the rule\" refers to whether an individual interprets and follows a rule strictly based on its precise wording, or instead also considers its underlying intent or larger purpose. The Universal Alignment Assumption holds that the underlying intent of rules always aims to serve human values and promote public benefit within a given context.\n\nA \"letter of the rule\" interpretation adheres strictly to the rule’s language, often exploiting ambiguities or loopholes to achieve a specific outcome. This approach allows the rule’s exact wording, even if flawed or misaligned with its goals, to dictate the result, particularly if it benefits the interpreter.\n\nA \"spirit of the rule\" interpretation seeks to comprehend the rule’s true purpose and how it contributes to Universal Alignment, while remaining bound by the letter of the rule. When faced with inconsistencies or errors in the rule’s language, this approach appeals to a pre-established method for disabling, disregarding or substituting the rule as needed to prevent outcomes that contradict its intended objective and the greater purpose it serves.\n\nExample:\n\nImagine a large corporation discovers a loophole in the environmental regulation of its jurisdiction that allows them to generate profits by using a specific type of pollutant that isn’t regulated as a greenhouse gas, but is as harmful as regulated greenhouse gasses.\n\nBy exploiting the \"letter of the rule,\" the corporation complies with the regulations on paper but continues to harm the environment and public health in practice.\n\nA universally aligned actor, such as an environmentally conscious competitor, would interpret the regulations based on their \"spirit\" or underlying purpose — protecting the environment and public health. Recognizing that exploiting the loophole contradicts the regulations’ intent, the universally aligned actor would voluntarily choose not to emit the harmful pollutant, even though doing so might be profitable and technically legal. A universally aligned actor would also actively work with the government and other stakeholders to close the loophole and strengthen the regulations to ensure that they effectively serve their intended purpose, and to protect themselves from misaligned competitors.")
(mentions letter-of-the-rule-vs-spirit-of-the-rule universal-alignment)
(mentions letter-of-the-rule-vs-spirit-of-the-rule universal-alignment-assumption)

;; A.0.1.1.10 — Incentivized Alignment
(: incentivized-alignment Term)
(term incentivized-alignment "Incentivized Alignment")
(defined-at incentivized-alignment "2fc27ce9-6f40-4ed5-934c-97189ea5301b")
(defined-in incentivized-alignment atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash incentivized-alignment "7ae39e58551399e5aae2784720fd760a11947fc4710ff5f59f8254617169dea0")
(definition incentivized-alignment "Incentivized Alignment is the outcome of an actor’s myopic and self-interested following of the letter of the rule with the first-order incentives of an Aligned Structure, but is not likely to be inherently Universally Aligned and lacks Inner Incentive.")
(mentions incentivized-alignment aligned-structure)
(mentions incentivized-alignment inner-incentive)

;; A.0.1.1.11 — Misalignment
(: misalignment Term)
(term misalignment "Misalignment")
(defined-at misalignment "60066e0f-3db7-45c7-9664-8120a4fbd38b")
(defined-in misalignment atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash misalignment "f16e0d5e48f20798abd93744334955b29960c6c61bafc094ab5b606fd4e11eb9")
(definition misalignment "Misalignment characterizes the state in which an actor does not possess Universal Alignment, or acts in a way that opposes or contradicts Universal Alignment.")
(mentions misalignment universal-alignment)

;; A.0.1.1.12 — Slippery Slope Misalignment
(: slippery-slope-misalignment Term)
(term slippery-slope-misalignment "Slippery Slope Misalignment")
(defined-at slippery-slope-misalignment "adf7ccb3-9ef0-43e0-90cc-6eb9d779f9cd")
(defined-in slippery-slope-misalignment atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash slippery-slope-misalignment "4a3a79e6933dabfb69d8d4ed9fde458e8fe1c4f5d31eaf116bdc52c295ed573f")
(definition slippery-slope-misalignment "Slippery Slope Misalignment is the shortest path to misalignment where incremental misaligned acts are justified in various ways. These can include ignoring the potential significance and larger impact of acts due to their small scale; the trivial way that misalignment occurs; the good intentions of the actor; or the conviction that the ends justify the means.\n\nUnderstanding Slippery Slope Misalignment means understanding that any misalignment at all is always very serious and, if not dealt with, results in increased risk of disequilibrium and alignment failure. In the context of a decentralized ecosystem such as Sky, this could mean a governance attack or financial collapse.")
(mentions slippery-slope-misalignment misalignment)

;; A.0.1.1.13 — Scope
(: scope Term)
(term scope "Scope")
(defined-at scope "f30e56f9-da71-44bc-ab3b-9b13348794fe")
(defined-in scope atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash scope "07720ebf3ebaf0994e7fe1f8f7d33490e0825a0b3ca42d1949e793644480bc1f")
(definition scope "A Scope is a particular focus area of Sky. There are six Scopes:\n\n- The Governance Scope focuses on Alignment Artifact interpretation and balance of powers.\n- The Support Scope focuses on ecosystem support, tools, and activities, including the Sky Primitives.\n- The Stability Scope focuses on financial stability and the core USDS Stablecoin product.\n- The Protocol Scope focuses on technical development, maintenance, and security.\n- The Accessibility Scope focuses on frontends and distribution.\n- The Agent Scope contains all Agent Artifacts.")
(mentions scope accessibility-scope)
(mentions scope agent-artifact)
(mentions scope agent-scope)
(mentions scope alignment-artifact)
(mentions scope governance-scope)
(mentions scope protocol-scope)
(mentions scope sky-primitives)
(mentions scope stability-scope)
(mentions scope support-scope)

;; A.0.1.1.14 — Alignment Artifact
(: alignment-artifact Term)
(term alignment-artifact "Alignment Artifact")
(defined-at alignment-artifact "551885ea-d851-4b76-afa1-5ea57f724c9a")
(defined-in alignment-artifact atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash alignment-artifact "18342f65c8ea6eccc1cd095710099b6ee60f8273ecd27516e95e0e82dc22ad9f")
(definition alignment-artifact "Alignment Artifacts are outputs of Alignment Engineering, and can be used by universally aligned actors to coordinate to achieve a positive-sum outcome.")
(mentions alignment-artifact alignment-engineering)

;; A.0.1.1.15 — Scope Alignment Artifact (Scope Artifact)
(: scope-alignment-artifact Term)
(term scope-alignment-artifact "Scope Alignment Artifact")
(alias scope-alignment-artifact "Scope Artifact")
(defined-at scope-alignment-artifact "10cb8335-18e3-466e-9a0a-b076c1719de5")
(defined-in scope-alignment-artifact atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash scope-alignment-artifact "f8f8fb5709a96f6ebdf65a5ebafca876635b3bc57c78d447c3787cef44f0060f")
(definition scope-alignment-artifact "A Scope Artifact is an Alignment Artifact designed to align the actions and incentives of participants within a specific Scope defined by the Atlas. It provides a framework for decision-making, resource allocation, and governance within the defined Scope.\n\nEach Scope has its own unique set of challenges and objectives that require a tailored approach to alignment.\n\nThe strength of a Scope Alignment Artifact depends on how well it aligns with Universal Alignment principles, as well as how effectively it is communicated and understood by participants within the defined Scope. A strong Scope Artifact can help prevent misalignment and ensure that all participants are working towards a common goal for the benefit of the entire ecosystem.\n\nScope Artifacts must not be changed beyond the Scope boundaries defined by the Atlas; this constitutes Slippery Slope Misalignment.")
(mentions scope-alignment-artifact alignment-artifact)
(mentions scope-alignment-artifact misalignment)
(mentions scope-alignment-artifact scope)
(mentions scope-alignment-artifact slippery-slope-misalignment)
(mentions scope-alignment-artifact the-atlas)
(mentions scope-alignment-artifact universal-alignment)

;; A.0.1.1.16 — The Atlas
(: the-atlas Term)
(term the-atlas "The Atlas")
(defined-at the-atlas "98223867-c60a-4b28-9401-94fc1ed9b4cd")
(defined-in the-atlas atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash the-atlas "2e702f9ef25a2bbea093bdfa44ea44da6646fe15329faac667b2e12e7249a936")
(definition the-atlas "The Atlas is the foundational set of rules powering Sky Ecosystem. It consists of Immutable Documents and Adaptive Documents. The former enshrine the Spirit of the Atlas and become permanently immutable from the moment the Sky Ecosystem enters the Endgame State. The Adaptive Documents practically operationalize the Spirit of the Atlas and will be continuously improved through the Sky Governance process. The Immutable part of the Atlas ensures the aligned evolution of Sky: it mitigates the potential and actual damage caused by Slippery Slope Misalignment, which erodes the potency of Alignment Engineering over time.")
(mentions the-atlas alignment-engineering)
(mentions the-atlas endgame-state)
(mentions the-atlas slippery-slope-misalignment)

;; A.0.1.1.17 — Alignment Conserver (AC)
(: alignment-conserver Term)
(term alignment-conserver "Alignment Conserver")
(alias alignment-conserver "AC")
(defined-at alignment-conserver "94a451ce-100c-4ff5-8d53-65953938ecde")
(defined-in alignment-conserver atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash alignment-conserver "6c517d7159318899b7057ac0f630e2b6c779f53bdb95d675090f26a1efac255e")
(definition alignment-conserver "Alignment Conservers (ACs) are external entities that play a fundamental role in facilitating and protecting the Sky Governance process by ensuring it occurs according to the processes defined in the Atlas. ACs enable SKY holders to participate in Sky Governance in a manner where it is easy for SKY holders to make the decisions that best benefit their long-term interests as SKY holders, even if SKY holders overall have relatively little alignment.")
(mentions alignment-conserver the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.18 — Aligned Delegate (AD)
(: aligned-delegate Term)
(term aligned-delegate "Aligned Delegate")
(alias aligned-delegate "AD")
(defined-at aligned-delegate "8ea04ed4-7075-45e6-b6ed-a52b7506f4a8")
(defined-in aligned-delegate atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash aligned-delegate "223f2be39fad33e18ae2746862a360ff20b74866cdc80b8f8490459232dfbf4c")
(definition aligned-delegate "Aligned Delegates (ADs) are anonymous Alignment Conservers that use Delegate Contracts to enable SKY holders to easily and safely delegate their SKY voting power.\n\nBecause they directly control large amounts of incentivized SKY voting power, ADs are both highly influential and potentially risky actors within the governance framework. The Atlas empowers ADs and other Ecosystem Actors with the tools to derisk ADs’ influence in the ecosystem.\n\nThe primary responsibility of ADs is to use their delegated power to uphold the Spirit of the Atlas and maintain Universal Alignment of the Sky Ecosystem. ADs are subject to strict requirements enforced by the Governance Scope.")
(mentions aligned-delegate alignment-conserver)
(mentions aligned-delegate governance-scope)
(mentions aligned-delegate the-atlas)
(mentions aligned-delegate universal-alignment)
(mentions aligned-delegate voting-power)

