(content-hash implicit-incentives "64354862e01236ff067de80e24976127b73ae51146f386431c9003204e077928")
(definition implicit-incentives "Implicit Incentives are the motivations or benefits that an actor can infer based on a ‘letter of the rules’ interpretation of an Alignment Artifact, and an assessment of the likelihood that these rules will be enforced.")
(mentions implicit-incentives alignment-artifact)

;; A.0.1.1.30 — Incentive Slack
(: incentive-slack Term)
(term incentive-slack "Incentive Slack")
(defined-at incentive-slack "133c6032-0082-4644-a3d5-87bcf5b30249")
(defined-in incentive-slack atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash incentive-slack "32b3d13707be9bed3ffa74bf163f7b7e7d100c442d2eb153cca4eceef02898b8")
(definition incentive-slack "Incentive Slack refers to the discrepancy between the explicit incentives (those clearly defined and communicated) and the implicit incentives (those inferred by actors) within an Aligned Structure. Incentive Slack can arise when coded rules are either not enforced or are too restrictive or impractical, leading to a pattern of bypassing these rules. When Incentive Slack is high, it creates the perception that rules are likely to be ignored, without regard for the spirit of the rules. This results in a significant risk of widespread misalignment. Incentive Slack cannot occur in an Aligned Structure in which actors are universally aligned and actively enforcing the rules.")
(mentions incentive-slack aligned-structure)
(mentions incentive-slack explicit-incentives)
(mentions incentive-slack implicit-incentives)
(mentions incentive-slack misalignment)

;; A.0.1.1.31 — Whole Weeks
(: whole-weeks Term)
(term whole-weeks "Whole Weeks")
(defined-at whole-weeks "20f8b661-37c0-4d16-9238-d9595bbcb4cf")
(defined-in whole-weeks atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash whole-weeks "d633547f0eb1f4e823948b3b72c40312dd5cbf14764449244c27599966eb7ad5")
(definition whole-weeks "The Atlas defines quarterly and yearly cycles that determine fixed points in time by counting whole weeks from the beginning of a quarter. The first whole week of a quarter is defined as the first week in which all days, beginning with Monday, fall within the quarter. Another definition would be \"the week starting with the first Monday of the quarter.\"")
(mentions whole-weeks the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.32 — SKY Staking
(: sky-staking Term)
(term sky-staking "SKY Staking")
(defined-at sky-staking "6a2c7245-8d67-4de0-80af-ce953352e1bb")
(defined-in sky-staking atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash sky-staking "2c82283dc21da01ab94aa16c611e36a156172d63ce4b2f39ab7986289e528e86")
(definition sky-staking "When a user stakes their SKY tokens, they receive Staking Rewards. Staked SKY can be freely unstaked at any time. SKY Staking also allows users to borrow USDS against their SKY at the SKY Borrow Rate.")

;; A.0.1.1.33 — Skylink
(: skylink Term)
(term skylink "Skylink")
(defined-at skylink "f0de89da-576a-4710-982e-40acf7f065cc")
(defined-in skylink atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash skylink "52522ba82b63ededfafbca87d95904a622cc983e4ce31f137b3dddef77e91d8d")
(definition skylink "Skylink is the Sky Ecosystem’s multichain solution, connecting USDS, SKY and other Sky Ecosystem tokens from the Ethereum Mainnet to other chains and L2 protocols. Skylink will make all core Sky features available on the chains and L2s it is deployed to, including Native USDS; Native Sky Savings Rate; Native Token Rewards and Native 1:1 conversion between USDC and USDS.")

;; A.0.1.1.34 — Target Document
(: target-document Term)
(term target-document "Target Document")
(defined-at target-document "575ab954-d26c-460e-8a11-ebe7f5586dff")
(defined-in target-document atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash target-document "eb0efd24fe0da3da73141813be3109de7b9fcc90136e6882bea2bde305a30b40")
(definition target-document "The term \"Target Document\" refers to the Immutable or Primary Document to which a Supporting Document is attached. Supporting Documents have various functions, including providing expanded definitions of vague or ambiguous terms in their Target Document; and providing hypothetical fact-patterns to illustrate the practical application of their Target Document. See [A.1.2.2.1.3 - Supporting Document Category](e87b6850-3792-495d-9460-0ac069a217e6).")

;; A.0.1.1.35 — Voting Power
(: voting-power Term)
(term voting-power "Voting Power")
(defined-at voting-power "44221aff-ad7c-41d3-a861-8a30963054fa")
(defined-in voting-power atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash voting-power "a58a9235d66a59b96eb3867f272c4b91bd789dd5d3f94780f10d3c6350b5bf8d")
(definition voting-power "\"Voting Power\" denotes the ability of Aligned Delegates to vote on Sky governance decisions on behalf of a SKY holder. SKY holders can delegate their Voting Power to an Aligned Delegate through Delegate Contracts, allowing the Aligned Delegate to vote on their behalf while the SKY holders retain control of their tokens.")
(mentions voting-power aligned-delegate)

;; A.0.1.1.36 — stUSDS
(: stusds Term)
(term stusds "stUSDS")
(defined-at stusds "591e1ba4-1f3e-44ac-9f4c-3f5d680f33d4")
(defined-in stusds atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash stusds "1a05b51153000adc1a3b6f607a7522cb7ec3714d03998c75f8279177a334111b")
(definition stusds "The token used to provide the capital for SKY Staking leverage is called stUSDS. It ensures that all SKY-backed borrowing is funded by segregated risk capital. Users can deposit USDS into a smart contract and receive stUSDS, which can later be converted back to USDS as long as there is unutilized USDS in the stUSDS converter smart contract.")
(mentions stusds sky-staking)

;; A.0.1.1.37 — Unrewarded USDS
(: unrewarded-usds Term)
(term unrewarded-usds "Unrewarded USDS")
(defined-at unrewarded-usds "86977920-c857-4a86-91ac-1a7571137c18")
(defined-in unrewarded-usds atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash unrewarded-usds "d3f16de366af37be50b91b9f11a587f326e35b52d0373bb5da9324166839cc70")
(definition unrewarded-usds "Unrewarded USDS are USDS balances that are not receiving the Sky Savings Rate, Integration Boost or USDS Token Rewards. USDS Token Rewards include both SKY and Agent token rewards.")
(mentions unrewarded-usds agent)

;; A.0.1.1.38 — Sky Forum
(: sky-forum Term)
(term sky-forum "Sky Forum")
(defined-at sky-forum "e78e8fbb-0602-4e67-8c44-88b1f0b30704")
(defined-in sky-forum atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash sky-forum "f53ec3b1053bbd336a2ac06c1fc666013ecbdf10fb5d49af949cf891d95f551b")
(definition sky-forum "The Sky Forum serves as a dedicated platform for governance across the Sky Ecosystem. Community members submit proposals, engage in debate, and align on decisions. Posts are organized by category according to subject matter. For example, proposals or discussions concerning Sky Core must use the \"Sky Core\" category, while those pertaining to Primes must use the Prime category associated with the Agent. Authors should also apply relevant tags to improve discoverability and cross-referencing. The forum is located at [https://forum.skyeco.com/](https://forum.skyeco.com/).")
(mentions sky-forum agent)

;; A.0.1.1.39 — Agent
(: agent Term)
(term agent "Agent")
(defined-at agent "3c18e6a7-95b8-44e9-8da6-1eadf3fdd356")
(defined-in agent atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash agent "e8993a22ac7fdc05404fe2bd8c3c57c2c0a584eb238f7a8a7d3595992f9ab524")
(definition agent "Agents are first-class economic citizens of Sky that autonomously pursue business opportunities. Each Agent has its own Agent Artifact and token. Initially, the creation of an Agent results in a Proto-Agent, which lacks any specialized role. To gain functionality within the Sky ecosystem, a Proto-Agent must deploy a special Transformation Primitive to transform into a specific Agent sub-type. The Agent sub-types currently defined in the Atlas include 1) Prime Agent and 2) Executor Agent, with the Executor Agent sub-type further divided into Operational Executor Agents and Core Executor Agents.\n\nAlthough Executor Agents are not yet operational, the Atlas nonetheless defines the foundational rules, processes, and governance structures necessary for their eventual activation. In the medium to long term, these Executor Agents will become fully operative and perform an essential function in facilitating the activities of Prime Agents across the Sky ecosystem.")
(mentions agent agent-artifact)
(mentions agent executor-agent)
(mentions agent operational-executor-agent)
(mentions agent prime-agent)
(mentions agent the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.40 — Agent Artifact
(: agent-artifact Term)
(term agent-artifact "Agent Artifact")
(defined-at agent-artifact "8d081c1a-6393-4aaf-8914-8959cdf2fee3")
(defined-in agent-artifact atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash agent-artifact "b678a37242f1ba1c49c56ff21eea7cf326df602b2a102b38d09ae85b5b68df89")
(definition agent-artifact "Agent Artifacts contain all rules, processes, parameters, and knowledge of the Agent. Agent Artifacts must be aligned with, and are fully subordinate to, the Sky Core Atlas.")
(mentions agent-artifact agent)

;; A.0.1.1.41 — Agent Scope
(: agent-scope Term)
(term agent-scope "Agent Scope")
(defined-at agent-scope "87dafa99-c36e-4e68-ac19-fccac4b3834d")
(defined-in agent-scope atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash agent-scope "468eaa3bb4b97b5a6f13700104f4f8a95038d6ea9c39eab138f427bc84c45f4d")
(definition agent-scope "The Agent Scope codifies all Agent Artifacts.")
(mentions agent-scope agent-artifact)

;; A.0.1.1.42 — Prime Agent
(: prime-agent Term)
(term prime-agent "Prime Agent")
(defined-at prime-agent "a8454271-c090-4084-b022-4430e3def93c")
(defined-in prime-agent atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash prime-agent "c9ed6ceaba2843585bac56b2574b5ef886b60a5549926b329ecc00b0d435c4ea")
(definition prime-agent "Prime Agents maintain and automate Sky features in new markets, and innovate custom products. Prime Agents are the only Agent type that can access all Sky Primitives; whereas Executor Agents are limited in the Primitives they can access.\n\n- Prime Agents cannot directly operationalize those elements of their strategies that directly interface with the Sky Protocol or shared ecosystem infrastructure. For such protocol-level and ecosystem-critical operations, Prime Agents must rely on Operational Executor Agents for implementation.\n- When a Prime Agent formulates a new initiative, it encodes the relevant instructions and parameters into its Agent Artifact. Insofar as the Prime Agent’s Artifact requires protocol-level interactions, the Operational Executors use the Artifact as a detailed operational blueprint for implementing the Prime Agent’s directives—ensuring consistency with the Atlas and minimizing risk.\n- This ensures a robust division between Prime Agents’ strategic, externally facing activities and the specialized operational activities that directly interface with Sky’s core systems.")
(mentions prime-agent agent)
(mentions prime-agent agent-artifact)
(mentions prime-agent executor-agent)
(mentions prime-agent operational-executor-agent)
(mentions prime-agent sky-primitives)
(mentions prime-agent the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.43 — Executor Agent
(: executor-agent Term)
(term executor-agent "Executor Agent")
(defined-at executor-agent "ac514975-66ad-4b43-8f76-42cac5ca599d")
(defined-in executor-agent atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash executor-agent "3ac1b29964d2df7c84f2c42980210c6b80e44231595b0caa46a9aae073a04daf")
(definition executor-agent "Executor Agents (\"Executors\") are specialized Agents that implement those elements of a Prime Agent’s activities that directly interface with the Sky Protocol or shared ecosystem resources, leaving Prime Agents free to focus on strategic, business development, and marketing efforts. There are two Executor sub-types: Core Executor Agents (\"Core Executor Agents\") and Operational Executor Agents (\"Operational Executors\").\n\n- Operational Executor Agents handle the day-to-day execution of those portions of a Prime Agent’s strategies that directly interface with the Sky Protocol, strictly following the instructions laid out in each Prime Agent’s Artifact. Prime Agents cannot be active in the Sky Ecosystem unless they have an active \"Operational Executor Accord\" which codifies their relationship with an Operational Executor. Operational Executors take on the risk of Prime Agents’ outcomes by providing collateralized insurance against losses or liabilities. Operational Executor Agents’ Operational Collateral can also cover losses from negligence or malicious behavior by the Operational Executor in carrying out the Prime Agent’s strategy.\n- Core Executor Agents, on the other hand, oversee the activities of Operational Executors, ensuring that the implementation of Prime Agent strategies aligns with the Atlas.\n- By separating strategy from operations, this division of labor empowers Prime Agents to innovate rapidly and expand their ventures without needing to develop specialized operational expertise, as Operational Executors manage the day-to-day technical implementation under the oversight of Core Executor Agents.")
(mentions executor-agent agent)
(mentions executor-agent operational-executor-agent)
(mentions executor-agent prime-agent)
(mentions executor-agent the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.44 — Operational Executor Agent
(: operational-executor-agent Term)
(term operational-executor-agent "Operational Executor Agent")
(defined-at operational-executor-agent "23253343-23e3-440f-90c0-43d3437c2098")
(defined-in operational-executor-agent atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash operational-executor-agent "d2d49d88ace61817237e0b2fcc3390e8e875a897d90d069f68d2e3776d143937")
(definition operational-executor-agent "Operational Executor Agents (\"Operational Executors\") are specialized Executor Agents tasked with implementing and verifying those elements of a Prime Agent’s strategy that directly interface with the Sky Protocol or shared ecosystem resources. While Prime Agents autonomously set strategic direction, Operational Executors are responsible for operationalizing those activities that modify on-chain or protocol-level state, relying on the relevant Primitive Configuration Documents in the Agent Artifact.\n\nEach Operational Executor Agent must comprise at least one Facilitator and at least one GovOps actor. Facilitators are responsible for interpreting the Atlas and the Agent Artifact and instructing GovOps actors to carry out the corresponding actions. To ensure accountability and mitigate potential risks, Operational Executor Agents must maintain Operational Collateral, which serves as a guarantee to cover losses or damages resulting from negligence or malicious behavior by either Facilitators or GovOps actors.")
(mentions operational-executor-agent agent-artifact)
(mentions operational-executor-agent executor-agent)
(mentions operational-executor-agent facilitator)
(mentions operational-executor-agent govops)
(mentions operational-executor-agent prime-agent)
(mentions operational-executor-agent the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.45 — Core Council Executor Agent
(: core-council-executor-agent Term)
(term core-council-executor-agent "Core Council Executor Agent")
(defined-at core-council-executor-agent "2a440474-20d1-4703-a57b-35e0cebb881c")
(defined-in core-council-executor-agent atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash core-council-executor-agent "326a684206dbd8969efb9aff018ce022c6750f061c0eb5fb70550f9d6ce10f79")
(definition core-council-executor-agent "Core Council Executor Agents (\"Core Executor Agents\") are Executor Agents who serve on the Core Council and act as checks on Operational Executor Agents.")
(mentions core-council-executor-agent core-council)
(mentions core-council-executor-agent executor-agent)
(mentions core-council-executor-agent operational-executor-agent)

;; A.0.1.1.46 — Core Council
(: core-council Term)
(term core-council "Core Council")
(defined-at core-council "5a03a0c4-a47a-409c-9b23-52ac93e63d45")
(defined-in core-council atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash core-council "ea0b7132231110e06a6ae81f5ab75397468f992bfb5fe7a6021a3019ec369ccc")
(definition core-council "The Core Council is a group of Executors responsible for operationalizing the protocol at the Sky Core level. It monitors Operational Executor compliance and enforces the Sky Core Atlas. It also oversees Sky Core governance processes, evolves the Risk Framework, monitors Alignment Conservers, and addresses governance disputes. The Council begins with a single seat held by Core Council Executor Agent 1 and will expand over time to multiple elected seats on a rotational basis, targeting up to seven members in the long term.")
(mentions core-council alignment-conserver)
(mentions core-council core-council-executor-agent)

;; A.0.1.1.47 — GovOps
(: govops Term)
(term govops "GovOps")
(defined-at govops "1e73ee4b-823d-406a-af54-223b43bc8e42")
(defined-in govops atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash govops "a997a6c7dafabc37b6d22484aba70f6430a6d07e6996750a1e04a28a007353b5")
(definition govops "Governance Operations (\"GovOps\") actors are specialized Ecosystem Actors operating within Executor Agent entities. They manage the technical implementation of Prime Agents’ Instances of Sky Primitives by carrying out on-chain/off-chain tasks necessary for Prime Agents’ operational and governance processes. They work in tandem with Executor Facilitators, who interpret the Atlas and the Agent Artifact.")
(mentions govops agent-artifact)
(mentions govops executor-agent)
(mentions govops facilitator)
(mentions govops prime-agent)
(mentions govops sky-primitives)
(mentions govops the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.48 — Operational Executor GovOps
(: operational-executor-govops Term)
(term operational-executor-govops "Operational Executor GovOps")
(defined-at operational-executor-govops "80c7e2e1-a2af-47dd-80c7-aee6823cca91")
(defined-in operational-executor-govops atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash operational-executor-govops "84b13af618a12d0b066fbe74fc7309ea947555ec44a31fca900a9f7deb195e31")
(definition operational-executor-govops "Operational Executor GovOps (\"Operational GovOps\") actors are GovOps actors that operate within Operational Executor Agents. Operational GovOps play a crucial role in implementing Prime Agent strategies, doing so by executing the technical specifications outlined in Primitive Configuration Documents of Agent Artifacts.")
(mentions operational-executor-govops agent-artifact)
(mentions operational-executor-govops govops)
(mentions operational-executor-govops operational-executor-agent)
(mentions operational-executor-govops prime-agent)

;; A.0.1.1.49 — Core Council GovOps
(: core-council-govops Term)
(term core-council-govops "Core Council GovOps")
(defined-at core-council-govops "e512e890-629f-450f-a14d-a3ea06a369c0")
(defined-in core-council-govops atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash core-council-govops "33adc7aa9e0f63421553179ff80264632c83f1511ffc8d52671269a4e31cd20b")
(definition core-council-govops "Core Council GovOps (\"Core GovOps\") actors are GovOps actors that operate within Core Executor Agents.")
(mentions core-council-govops executor-agent)
(mentions core-council-govops govops)

;; A.0.1.1.50 — Operational Executor Facilitator
(: operational-executor-facilitator Term)
(term operational-executor-facilitator "Operational Executor Facilitator")
(defined-at operational-executor-facilitator "2d984fe4-c1d7-4ac3-835b-19f19a3a5505")
(defined-in operational-executor-facilitator atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash operational-executor-facilitator "ae2a91e213534a73bdf77d757109592c506c6f006f24472713d871f2ecce9c47")
(definition operational-executor-facilitator "Operational Executor Facilitators are Facilitators that interpret Artifacts and the Atlas on behalf of Operational Executor Agents.")
(mentions operational-executor-facilitator facilitator)
(mentions operational-executor-facilitator operational-executor-agent)
(mentions operational-executor-facilitator the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.51 — Core Council Executor Facilitator
(: core-council-executor-facilitator Term)
(term core-council-executor-facilitator "Core Council Executor Facilitator")
(defined-at core-council-executor-facilitator "453e9bfb-2776-486d-b451-35742e49e0ab")
(defined-in core-council-executor-facilitator atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash core-council-executor-facilitator "a83dbee1f627ccd3eb92f5db781e76485358513d0ec49d7b63bcf01e12b8abdb")
(definition core-council-executor-facilitator "Core Council Executor Facilitators (\"Core Facilitator\") interpret Artifacts and the Atlas on behalf of Core Executor Agents.")
(mentions core-council-executor-facilitator executor-agent)
(mentions core-council-executor-facilitator facilitator)
(mentions core-council-executor-facilitator the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.52 — Sky Primitives
(: sky-primitives Term)
(term sky-primitives "Sky Primitives")
(defined-at sky-primitives "ae14941a-635e-4022-af4d-2bec2827fbbf")
(defined-in sky-primitives atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash sky-primitives "ab36a785311f753955748bfc2c39e783ea926557ac274c79a20b9316fefbb1fb")
(definition sky-primitives "Sky Primitives are the core building blocks of the Sky ecosystem, serving as the primary interface between Agents and the Atlas. By providing a standardized set of tools and interfaces, Sky Primitives empower Prime Agents to create, innovate, and evolve the Sky Protocol in a decentralized manner. The Sky Primitives are also used by Executor Agents, which serve as the robust and standardized intermediary layer between Prime Agents and the Sky Protocol.")
(mentions sky-primitives agent)
(mentions sky-primitives executor-agent)
(mentions sky-primitives prime-agent)
(mentions sky-primitives the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.53 — Conformance
(: conformance Term)
(term conformance "Conformance")
(defined-at conformance "cb66c28b-c05f-4ccc-ad44-f05aacf78b9c")
(defined-in conformance atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash conformance "8c366947c3d2ce0631cea864e8742e43f82019ed81bd7cb7a7baffbe0d372772")
(definition conformance "Conformance characterizes the state in which a Synome Document accurately operationalizes the principles, rules, and processes specified by the Atlas Documents.")
(mentions conformance the-atlas)

;; A.0.1.1.54 — Independent Governance
(: independent-governance Term)
(term independent-governance "Independent Governance")
(defined-at independent-governance "6e1c1d71-7f57-4842-9767-7de8f27a532a")
(defined-in independent-governance atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash independent-governance "adf4491367307981cbcc825ecf25ce108de5633e4fd1d457d23d816761143285")
(definition independent-governance "Independent Governance is the state of a Prime Agent that has a token and an established governance process by which the token's holders can produce binding decisions directing the Agent.")
(mentions independent-governance agent)
(mentions independent-governance prime-agent)

;; A.0.1.1.55 — Sky Frontier Foundation
(: sky-frontier-foundation Term)
(term sky-frontier-foundation "Sky Frontier Foundation")
(defined-at sky-frontier-foundation "05d714e5-9428-4978-ac57-e3885b4e4c41")
(defined-in sky-frontier-foundation atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash sky-frontier-foundation "7c8469cf0eeb3e770bc2ca211f8bd0e6d4bf43e66100bf0860ec21023db13d5d")
(definition sky-frontier-foundation "The Sky Frontier Foundation is a foundation that supports the innovation, development, and acceleration of the Sky Ecosystem. Its mandate is to fund public goods infrastructure and self-sustainable activities to support long-term ecosystem growth.\n\nThe Sky Frontier Foundation's multisig address is `0xca5183FB9997046fbd9bA8113139bf5a5Af122A0`.")

;; A.0.1.1.56 — Fortification Foundation
(: fortification-foundation Term)
(term fortification-foundation "Fortification Foundation")
(defined-at fortification-foundation "f44e6bf3-acf2-483e-af99-7cbee48c0c56")
(defined-in fortification-foundation atlas-preamble-definitions)
(content-hash fortification-foundation "4376e835e7baf5b4075dbbea9f302db724c81d009e1e4eb193277b6b601c9c9f")
(definition fortification-foundation "The Fortification Foundation is a foundation that addresses existential, long-term legal and political issues of the Sky Ecosystem. Its responsibilities include legal defense, IP protection, regulatory engagement, resilience, and unquantifiable risk management.")
